    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_0f9c6b4dbdd16e4ad14adca9587d45d63b7629668859c1ca0c82bdd8e65421cf",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Family symmetry is diagnosed by two coupled averaging laws rather than by root number alone: root-number expectations select functional-equation branches, while the declared coefficient measure determines local correlations and whether the polar product contains only strict pairs or also diagonal pairs, yielding the unitary, orthogonal, or symplectic moment geometry in the source's examples.",
