      "proposed_content": "The derivative-defined log conductor provides a common local spectral coordinate: it matches an L-function's zero density to matrix size, while family-specific re-expansions of functional-equation factors absorb archimedean corrections into the conductor exponential and leave them to reappear in lower polynomial coefficients.",
