      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a0ec0140c2b6863b24a88cc8a681149c62609ed8b66e1f0c3041157d311d74da",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Multiplicative diagonal constraints split the moment expression into a universal singular layer and an arithmetic regular layer: extracted zeta-like poles control residue degree and symmetry-relevant pair geometry, while an analytic Euler product retains prime-local data and specializes at zero shift to the arithmetic part of the leading constant.",
